WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
Early in 2023, the first
official estimate came in:

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:07.230
America's GDP, measured in dollars,

3
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.490
grew 9.2 percent in 2022.

4
00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:14.880
The total reached 25.46 trillion dollars.

5
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.260
That is a lot of dollars.

6
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:21.320
But did Americans really
make 9.2 percent more stuff?

7
00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:24.540
More cars, more burgers, more haircuts?

8
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.840
So if a country's output is
worth more money this year,

9
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.110
has it really produced more?

10
00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:33.410
In this mission, you'll
add up GDP three ways:

11
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.440
spending, income and value added.

12
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.670
Then you'll value a tiny economy
that makes only pizzas and books,

13
00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:42.310
one year at a time.

14
00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.340
Your mission: figure out
when a bigger dollar figure

15
00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:47.490
means a country truly made more.
